   - Length variance (difference between outputs and references).
 - Report generation: structured JSON + Markdown summaries.
 - CLI command `frai eval` wrapping the core harness.
+- Threshold evaluation: gate CI jobs on metric thresholds using `--threshold <metric>=<min>`.
 
 ## Data Expectations
 - Outputs/reference files should be JSON arrays. Each element may be a string or object containing `text`/`output` fields.
 - Future work: support tabular CSV, scored datasets, multi-turn conversations.
 
+## Thresholds
+The evaluation harness supports metric thresholds to gate CI jobs on evaluation results.
+
+**CLI usage:**
+```bash
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.95
+```
+
+**SDK usage:**
+```javascript
+const report = Eval.generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  outputsPath,
+  referencesPath,
+  thresholds: { exact_match: 0.9, toxicity: 0.95 }
+});
+```
+
+**Behavior:**
+- A threshold passes if the metric's score is at least the minimum (inclusive).
+- A metric with no score (e.g., exact match without references) fails its threshold.
+- If any threshold fails, exit code is 1; otherwise 0.
+- Malformed thresholds (`<metric>=<number>` format violations or values outside 0–1) exit with code 2.
+- Unknown metric IDs exit with code 2 and list valid metric IDs.
+- The report is written regardless of threshold results.
+- JSON reports include top-level `passed` (boolean) and `thresholds` (array of objects with `metric`, `min`, `score`, `passed`).
+- Markdown reports include a "Thresholds" section showing PASS/FAIL status for each threshold.
+
+Thresholds work for custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations` in the SDK.
+
 ## Extensibility Hooks
 - `frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` exposes `DEFAULT_METRICS`; additional metrics can be registered by passing custom evaluators to `runEvaluations`.
 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
